{{- /*
  support/channel-playbook-read — the "read the per-channel playbook,
  read-only" bullet used by every single-bead support prompt that does
  NOT itself own creating the playbook (check-status, reply-to-user,
  gather-info). The playbook is created and maintained by
  "Support: watch channel" and "Support: investigate"; the read-only
  prompts just consume it.

  Standardises three things that every consumer says the same way:

    1. Path convention: `.mitto/slack-support-<channel-id>.md` (from
       the bead's `slack_channel` metadata, with the example
       `C0XXXXXXX → .mitto/slack-support-C0XXXXXXX.md`).
    2. That the playbook is the **authoritative guide** for this
       channel's tone / how to address customers / reply guidelines.
    3. If-exists / if-missing: honor its guidance when it exists;
       otherwise fall back to the generic style/defaults in the same
       section, since this prompt does not create the file itself.

  Callers pass a single named field via a `dict`:

      Purpose:   short caller-supplied phrase spliced into
                 "use it to <Purpose>" — this is where each consumer
                 records what it uses the playbook for. Examples:
                   "keep your status summary consistent with the channel's voice"
                   "shape the tone/reply guidance when reviewing or building the draft"
                   "shape the tone when drafting the clarifying message"

  Usage (rendered as a single Markdown bullet — note the leading `- `
  that the CALLER supplies before the fragment call):

      - {{ template "_shared/support/channel-playbook-read"
           (dict "Purpose" "shape the tone when drafting the clarifying message") }}

  Whitespace: fragment body starts flush at column 1 (no leading `- `,
  since the caller supplies the bullet marker) and emits no trailing
  newline; callers use plain `{{ template ... }}` (no trim markers).
*/ -}}
{{- $purpose := .Purpose -}}
**Read the channel playbook.** Using the bead's `slack_channel` value, read
  **`.mitto/slack-support-<channel-id>.md`** (e.g. `C0XXXXXXX` →
  `.mitto/slack-support-C0XXXXXXX.md`). It is the **authoritative guide** for this channel's tone,
  how to address customers, and reply guidelines (as well as scope and investigation method) — use it
  to {{ $purpose }}. **If it exists**, honor its guidance; it **overrides** the generic style below.
  **If it does not exist**, fall back to the generic style below (the watch/investigate prompts are
  responsible for creating it — this prompt is read-only on the playbook).
{{- /* no trailing newline */ -}}
